[5] read along the 60-degree rows, right to left, a keystone castle of width w is a composition (b_1, ..., b_w) of its cells with b_1 = 1 and 2 <= b_(i+1) <= b_i + 1 + (b_i mod 2), each once, w <= 6: True
[6] the up triangles of a keystone castle of width w, brick i of row t over bricks i and i + 1 of row t - 1, are a brick-wall castle of width w, each reached 2^f times, f the pairs of neighboring up triangles above the bottom row with no up triangle on the down triangle between them; all C_w brick-wall castles are reached; w <= 6: True
